# mindone 12.09 (F4136): audioserver reads a property under the generic (non-dedicated) vendor
# context vendor_default_prop - 1 read/open/getattr/map denial per boot
# (device/logs/catch-0911-185910/dmesg.txt.gz). Unlike default_prop/misctrl_prop/
# custom_version_prop (platform types, see mtk_hal_camera.te/mtk_hal_c2.te), vendor_default_prop
# belongs to the vendor - a plain allow here does not trip an AOSP neverallow (the restriction runs
# the other way: vendor domains must not touch PLATFORM types, not the reverse).
# 🔴 Not verified by a build (secilc is unavailable on the host, the full ROM build is currently busy
# with another track) - if the next build fails on this rule with libsepol.report_failure
# (signature in F3908), replace it with dontaudit following the mtk_hal_camera.te pattern.
# Which exact property is being read is not established (F4066, OPEN): 96 properties share this
# generic context, and telling them apart by live polling did not work.
# 12.09: allow coredomain -> vendor_default_prop violates neverallow (an internal vendor
# type); until a public property type exists, use dontaudit. Functionally unchanged in permissive.
# 🔴 14.09 18:25: the Q17 "correction" (get_prop -> vendor_default_prop) FAILED the build:
# 6 neverallow violations at system/sepolicy/{private,public}/property.te -- vendor_default_prop is a
# vendor-INTERNAL type and coredomain must not read it (F4444). Reverted to dontaudit, which is what the
# 12.09 note above already prescribed. This only silences the log line; the read itself was never needed
# (F4068: enforcing worked without it).
dontaudit audioserver vendor_default_prop:file { read open getattr map };
